<p class="byline">By <a href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">FiscalHour</a></p>
<p class="last-updated">Dates checked <time datetime="2026-11-20">November 20, 2026</time>. This page lists schedules. It is not a forecast, and it is not investment advice. <a href="{{ '/disclaimer/' | url }}">Read the disclaimer</a>.</p>

<p>Four releases sit on top of the week ahead, using only the dates those agencies had posted on 20 November 2026. On Wednesday 25 November the <a href="https://www.bea.gov/news/schedule/full">Bureau of Economic Analysis schedule</a> lists two 8:30 a.m. reports: the second estimate of third-quarter GDP, and personal income and outlays for October, which is the release that carries the PCE price index. The same morning is not a Freddie Mac Thursday. <a href="https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms/docs/PMMS_Publication_Calendar.pdf">Freddie Mac’s publication calendar</a> puts the next Primary Mortgage Market Survey on Wednesday 25 November, and the <a href="https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms">PMMS page</a> says the survey comes out at 12 p.m. ET, moving to Wednesday when a U.S. holiday falls on Thursday.</p>

<p>The next jobs report is the November Employment Situation. The <a href="https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/empsit.htm">BLS schedule</a> lists it for Friday 4 December at 8:30 a.m. The next CPI, also for November, is on the <a href="https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/cpi.htm">CPI schedule</a> for Thursday 10 December at 8:30 a.m. The October CPI, already out, is the one <a href="{{ '/articles/2026-11-11-october-cpi-0-4-percent-core-holds-0-3/' | url }}">FiscalHour reported at 0.4%</a>.</p>

<p>The <a href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/2026-december.htm">Board’s December calendar</a> lists a two-day FOMC meeting on 8-9 December, a 2:00 p.m. entry on the 9th, and a 2:30 p.m. press conference the same day. Minutes of that meeting are listed for 2:00 p.m. on 30 December. The <a href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm">FOMC calendar</a> marks the December meeting with the asterisk it uses for a Summary of Economic Projections. That asterisk is a label on the calendar, not a preview of the vote. The October meeting’s minutes, released 18 November, are covered in the <a href="{{ '/articles/2026-11-19-fomc-minutes-october-2026-rate-hike-ai-debt-financial-stability/' | url }}">minutes story</a>.</p>

