<p>BLS and BEA print “8:30 AM” on their schedules and do not label a time zone in those tables. The Federal Reserve’s December calendar prints 2:00 p.m. and 2:30 p.m. and does not label a zone either. Freddie Mac is the exception: its PMMS page says 12 p.m. ET. If a page and this table ever disagree, use the agency page. Schedules move, and this one does not update itself.</p>

