<p>The December FOMC meeting is the one with a clock time in this table, because the Board’s month calendar prints one. The year-page <a href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm">FOMC calendar</a> confirms the dates and the projections asterisk, and it says the page was last updated 18 November 2026. The December month page says it was last updated 24 June 2025, so the clock times are older than the year-page date list. Both are linked on purpose.</p>

<h2>How the mortgage week is counted</h2>
<p>Freddie Mac’s <a href="https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms">PMMS page</a> says the published average is not a quote from a single day. Applications count from 12:00 a.m. ET on the prior Thursday through 11:59 p.m. ET on Wednesday, and the average is released at noon ET. The 19 November survey, the latest one on the archive when this page was checked, is written up with the weekly path since early October in the <a href="{{ '/articles/2026-10-30-freddie-mac-mortgage-rates/' | url }}">mortgage-rate story</a>. A survey average is not the rate a particular borrower will be offered.</p>

